  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "How did we learn about the dinosaurs?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "We learned from fossils."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Fossils are the bodies of long-dead animals."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "But making a fossil takes a lot of time and luck."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "First, an animal needs to die."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Then, it must be covered in mud."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "The mud should dry slowly."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "If it dries too fast, this can destroy the fossil."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Also, nothing should touch the bones."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Finally, a fossil needs to age for 10,000 years to fully form."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "This is why fossils are so rare."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Only about one bone in a million becomes a fossil."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
